              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grassland\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Grassland\">Grassland</a> in 7th Brigade Park, Chermside, is of human creation (anthropogenic).  It was created over approximately a century (19th - 20th) for grazing, military purposes and sport, replacing the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/forest\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:forest\">forest</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/woodland\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:woodland\">woodland</a> that originally covered the district.  The grassland is maintained by regular mowing, without which it would slowly revert to forest.  The flora is a mix or native and exotic grasses, forbs and herbs, all of which are adapted to frequent mowing and slashing.",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
